{
  "id": "COMPOUND:26277 - PROTEIN:5702",
  "verbalization": "Stecholide I is implicated in the regulation of CCF-STTG1 through a series of molecular interactions involving sialyltransferases. The evidence suggests that Stecholide I acts as a target of multiple compounds, which in turn target CCF-STTG1. These compounds, including (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide, are known to interact with the sialyltransferase enzyme. This indicates that Stecholide I may modulate the activity of these compounds, which then influence CCF-STTG1. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Stecholide I could either directly or indirectly regulate CCF-STTG1 through its interaction with sialyltransferases. The evidence supports a role for Stecholide I in the regulation of CCF-STTG1 via a complex network of molecular interactions involving sialyltransferases and their target compounds.",
